This traceset describes the daily mobility of buses in the urban area
of Vannes (France). No radio transmission is assumed.

This is a synthetic yet realistic dataset: the mobility of each bus
has been produced by extracting the characteristics of the bus routes
from OpenStreetMap
(https://www.openstreetmap.org/#map=14/47.6556/-2.7565&layers=T), and
combining these routes with the bus company's timetables
(http://www.kiceo.fr, as of 2017).

The resulting dataset involves 60 buses covering the city, between
05:25 AM and 7h39 PM. These buses do not necessarily start and stop
running at the same time. Besides, a few of them only run at specific
periods during the day. These are typically school buses that
transport students to school or back home. The scenario therefore
exhibits moderate churn, as the number of running buses is not stable
over time.

A video showing the buses running in the city is available at
https://casa-irisa.univ-ubs.fr/download/videos/kiceo_large.mp4

Duration of the scenario   : 14h14' (from 05h25' to 19h39')
Nb of nodes (buses)        : 60 (total) / 56 (max active simultaneously)
Activity duration per node : 26’ / 14h08’ / 10h58’ / 3h26’ (*)


(* = min / max / avg / stdev values)

The data provided in this dataset describe a time-varying graph (TVG)
whose nodes model buses. This TVG is formatted according to the DGS file format
described below.

Files using this format can be processed by the GraphStream library
(https://graphstream-project.org), or by the LEPTON emulation platform
(https://casa-irisa.univ-ubs.fr/lepton).

The DGS file format specification is available in
https://graphstream-project.org/doc/Advanced-Concepts/The-DGS-File-Format.

Below are further details about how this format is used in this dataset:

- the timesteps are specified in milliseconds, starting at time
  0.

- timestep values are specified relatively to a reference time, which
  is specified as graph attribute 'ref_time=19500000' (i.e., 05:25 AM).

- node coordinates are updated every second. They are specified as x
  and y attributes (cartesian coordinates expressed in meters).

- all node coordinates are specified relatively to a reference point
  whose coordinates are specified in the graph attribute 'area' (in
  the file header). The value of this attribute is of the form
  'car:x,y,width,height:reflat,reflon', where (x,y) and
  (reflat,reflon) are the cartesian and geographical coordinates of
  the reference location point, and (width,height) determine
  the size of the area.

- each bus is identified as line-xx-yy, where xx is a bus line number
  (there are 11 bus lines), and yy is the bus number in that line
